  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Tuxedo. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Tuxedo is a card-capturing game invented by George Parker, played with a 56-card Rook deck (no Rook card). 4 cards per player + 4 face-up in the 'pond'. Capture by matching number or matching sums. Sweeps (clearing the pond) score bonus. 'Orange' call bonus for capturing red+yellow together. First to 100 wins.",
    objective: 'Score points by capturing cards (match number or sum to 14), sweeps, 5s, Orange call (red and yellow together), and most cards; first to 100 wins.',
    gameplay: "Play 1 card per turn. Capture matching number or cards summing to your card's value. Can't capture = play to pond. Sweeps: Big Sweep (4+ cards) = 10 pts. Little Sweep (3 or fewer) = 5 pts. Orange call: Red+Yellow captured = 10 bonus (must call 'Orange!'). 5-value cards = 5 pts each. Most cards = 15 pts.",
